body:
You can use Cobra error handling to avoid `utils.Check` here

```go
RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
  return createPr(args...)
}
```

Ideally, we would retire `utils.Check` since it terminates the main process on errors and therefore is ultimately non-testable through Go

Nit: in the interest of having a single `github.CreatePullRequest()` invocation per method (for the sake of readability/simplicity), would this approach make sense?

```go
prParams := github.PullRequestParams{
  // ...
}

if (interactive) {
  // go into survey mode, populate extra `prParams` fields
}

// convergence of both interactive and non-interactive mode
return github.CreatePullRequest(prParams)
```

**Edit:** aah I scrolled further and now I see your below comment:

> i expect that survey will intake slightly different data

That migth be true, but I still think we could have a single point of creation of pull requests. The data within the params struct will likely be different, but I don't see why the invocation style should be.

